# The sdist has to be self-sufficient: `pytest` collects tests/conftest.py and reads the
# frozen fixtures, the generator ledger and the committed example artifact; `selftest`
# reads data/synthetic/ + data/truth/. Without these the sdist extracts to a tree that
# cannot even collect (measured 2026-10-20: tests/conftest.py, tools/, data/ and examples/
# were all absent from the sdist).
#
# The wheel needs none of this -- it ships the package plus its JS mirror, and an installed
# `verify` works from any CWD. Only `selftest` needs the repository around it, and the
# README says so.
#
# NOTE: these are the *frozen* fixtures travelling with the package, not a place to
# regenerate them. `tools/gen_synthetic_series.py --check` stays the gate on their bytes;
# building an sdist from a CRLF working tree would break that ledger in the extracted tree.
include LICENSE
include README.md
include SKILL.md
include pyproject.toml
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tools *.py
recursive-include data *.csv *.json *.txt *.md
recursive-include examples *.html